## Output
Call `muse.finish_step` once with an `output` object. Do not write prose, analysis, or a summary outside that tool call. Keep reasons compact: for a pass, use an empty `reasons` list unless one short note is genuinely useful; for a fail or hold, give the smallest specific reason that lets the repair step act.
Return `results`, one object per lens: `lens`, `verdict` (`pass`, `fail`, or `hold`), `reasons`, `evidence_handles`, and `confidence` (`low`, `medium`, or `high`). Cite the handle or quote behind every fail/hold reason. If a lens cannot verify with available evidence, that lens is `hold` — never pass by benefit of the doubt.

