### Finding 1
Sakana AI released two orchestration models on Friday, September 11, 2026: Fugu Max and Fugu Ultra v2. Fugu Max is priced at $2/$6 per million input/output tokens, which the reporting frames as 40-60% below Claude Sonnet 5, GPT-6 Terra, and Kimi K3 output rates, and both models bill cached input at a flat $0.25/M regardless of context length. Both share the same routing architecture over a swappable pool of frontier and specialist LLMs. Fugu Max tops six benchmarks including Terminal-Bench 2.1, GPQAD, AA-LCR, GDP.pdf, AutomationBench, and SWEFish; Fugu Ultra v2 scores 48.3 on Chartography (visual reasoning) vs 27.3 for Opus 5 and 29.5 for Fable 5, and 74.3 on DeepSWE, notably without Fable 5, Fable 5.1, or GPT-6 Astra in its agent pool. The writeup calls this the second orchestration-beats-flagship datapoint this month after GitHub HydraFusion on Sept 4, and notes it is the first non-Chinese release to undercut Kimi K3's $6/M output on the axis Sonnet 5 anchors.
