### Finding 3
Anthropic's fourth threat intelligence report, published September 10, 2026 and covering December 2025 through August 2026, publicly names and documents specific Chinese AI companies — Alibaba, Moonshot, DeepSeek, Xiaomi, Z.ai, and MiniMax — operating industrial-scale covert campaigns to extract Claude's capabilities via fraudulent API accounts. This is the first time a frontier lab has publicly named the companies behind what Anthropic calls illicit distillation: using a more capable model's outputs, at industrial scale, covertly and without authorization, to train a second model. The Alibaba campaign alone operated through 3,500 fake accounts with stolen credit cards; the report defines illicit distillation as requiring fraud (fake accounts, stolen credentials, shared fixed prompts), distinguishing it from legitimate, authorized, disclosed distillation. The practical read for anyone running agents through third-party API aggregators or resellers: stolen API keys are now the primary AI IP-theft channel (not model-weight exfiltration), and detection requires usage-pattern and account-origin analysis most operators do not run.
